{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:425e31f3388d43b9","name":"Force Detector","source":{"id":"source:reference-425e31f3388d43b9","title":"Force Detector","revision":20421,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:48:42Z","sha256":"508204da545f7fc97cd7992eb7c1a1fcd3299b8f369a9a183df2b4f837fc5174","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20421","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Force%20Detector&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-425e31f3388d43b9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 2,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 9 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A blanket term used to cover a variety of devices, Force Detectors are pieces of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," designed to detect ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Sensitivity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Sensitivity","referenceId":"reference:5202cab02f367bcf"},", or the potential for it, within a living being. Force Detectors can take many forms; ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," used Force Detectors that relied on blood samples to determine midichlorian counts. During the height of the Empire, Force Detectors were built using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thaissen Crystals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thaissen_Crystals?action=edit&redlink=1"}," from the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mimban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mimban?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that glow in the presence of Force-users.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Regardless of the specific form, most Force Detectors function in a similar manner. Using a Force Detector requires 5 rounds and a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check to successfully activate the device. If the target of the Force Detector has the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Sensitivity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Sensitivity","referenceId":"reference:5202cab02f367bcf"}," feat, the Force Detector indicates that the target is Force-sensitive.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
